ontinuous growth rate is about 4.496% per year, which translates to an annual change of roughly 1,305 million dollars when continuously compounded.\n\nThe key is understanding that while the rate is unitless, it directly relates to the monetary value when applied to the initial amount.\n\nCalculating the rate involves a precise natural logarithm calculation: r = ln(29691/28386) / 1, which yields 0.04496. When rounded to the nearest thousandths, this becomes 0.045.\n","signature":""},{"type":"toolRequest","id":"call_1c4e903de05c43a797310103","toolCall":{"status":"success","value":{"name":"shell","arguments":{"command":"python3 -c \"\nimport math\ninitial = 28386\nfinal = 29691\nt = 1  # 1 year\nr = math.log(final / initial) / t\nprint(f'Initial: {initial} million dollars')\nprint(f'Final: {final} million dollars')\nprint(f'Ratio: {final/initial}')\nprint(f'ln(ratio): {math.log(final/initial)}')\nprint(f'Continuous rate of change: {r}')\nprint(f'Rounded to 3 decimal places: {round(r, 3)}')\n\""}}},"_meta":{"goose_extension":"developer"}}],"metadata":{"userVisible":true,"agentVisible":true}}}
